  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Southern Border’s Human Smoke Mountain Range holds the most living mortals in Southern Border. Villages cover the mountains, and some peaks hold several neighboring villages. At the center of that range sits the political core of the villages, Human Smoke Mountain, base of the super clan Chai clan.",
      "chapters": [
        1347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "fac_chai_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chai Fu founded Chai clan here in his later years. He cultivated fire path along with earth path, drew insight from The Legends of Ren Zu for a human path killer move, modified the mountain range, and created Human Smoke Mountain. In his era he was the number one person in Southern Border’s Gu Immortal world.",
      "chapters": [
        1347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_chai_fu",
        "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Because of the human path method’s limitation, the mortals around Chai clan cannot leave Human Smoke Mountain Range, so the clan needs an immortal Gu formation or an Immortal Gu House to defend them. Chai clan’s Human Smoke Mountain sits north of the spiral whirlpool where red dragon river and jade dragon river cross, with Ba clan south and Xia clan east.",
      "chapters": [
        1347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_formation",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "fac_ba_clan",
        "fac_xia_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Villages after villages cover the mountains of Human Smoke Mountain Range. On some peaks several villages stand as neighbors, and the population has multiplied to its limit.",
      "chapters": [
        1347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s rank eight subordinates Bing Yuan, Golden Fur Immortal Monarch, and Shi Zong come to Human Smoke Mountain, named as Chai clan’s headquarters, to buy Chai clan’s human path results: the killer move congregated human talent, the human path mountain Human Smoke Mountain, and many mortals raised by the clan. Shi Zong says the purchase is to kill those mortals. Golden Fur Immortal Monarch says the nurtured humans have abundant human qi and that Fang Yuan’s Human Sea only lacks the final step.",
      "chapters": [
        2137
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "trade-demand",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_bing_yuan",
        "char_golden_fur_immortal_monarch",
        "char_shi_zong",
        "loc_human_sea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Thousands of years earlier at Human Smoke Mountain, Chai Fu uses congregated human talent and the favorable location of Human Smoke Mountain to establish Chai clan. Fang Yuan later asks for congregated human talent, Human Smoke Mountain, and the outsider mortals Chai clan is nurturing, which the clan treats as excavating its core foundation.",
      "chapters": [
        2138
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-method",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the mountain is recently obtained, Fang Yuan keeps Human Smoke Mountain because he expects that continuing Chai clan’s human path research will let him condense its essence into an incomplete Human Mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        2142
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "essence-for-human-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_human_mountain"
      ]
    }
  ],
